# Everything under terraform/ is security-sensitive: the catalogue is the
# authorisation record, and every other file either enforces it or controls
# how it is enforced. Default the whole directory to the owning team rather
# than listing files, so a new .tf file is covered the moment it is added.
/terraform/               @Delta-SK/platform-engineering

# The backend, the OIDC trust policies, the team itself and the branch
# protection on this repository all live here. Changing any of them changes
# the controls.
/bootstrap/               @Delta-SK/platform-engineering

# The destroy guard and the repository-controls check run from here, and the
# apply job trusts them. Editing them is editing a control.
/scripts/                 @Delta-SK/platform-engineering

# The Terraform version every job and every engineer runs. Changing it
# changes the binary that holds the state.
/.terraform-version       @Delta-SK/platform-engineering

# CI is what enforces the GitOps flow. A change here can disable every other
# control in this repository, including the plan that would have shown it.
/.github/                 @Delta-SK/platform-engineering
